>>
endobj
229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Despite the advancement of mobile technology, personal safety for women remains a significant concern in many urban and isolated environments. The core problem lies in the inefficiency of traditional emergency response methods during high-stress situations.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Furthermore, many existing safety apps are either too complex for rapid use or lack integrated features like automatic evidence collection \(audio recording\) and real-time location broadcasting. This technological gap leaves women vulnerable during critical moments where every second counts. There is a clear need for a specialized system that bypasses these barriers to provide an instantaneous, discreet, and reliable lifeline to trusted contacts and authorities.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (3.Scope of Work)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (The SafeStep application focuses on providing emergency assistance features for women through a simple and reliable mobile platform. The system allows users to register their personal information and add trusted emergency contacts.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
